From e23ab638916d6aaabd7b59efbd436f96e74f6689 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 03:28:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] NewtonK0 method of the fixed point solver; findings of the
 short review

- FixedPointSolver, method NewtonK0: Newton's method, the consistent
  tangent operator (assembled or applied without assembly) being inverted
  by the conjugate gradient of MFEM preconditioned by the linear solver of
  the elastic operator, whose setup is kept (for instance BoomerAMG built
  once on K0); options of the conjugate gradient in TangentLinearSolver;
  the linear solver of the elastic operator is required and the method
  can't be accelerated;
- the elastic predictions use the linear solver provided by the non linear
  solver only for the BEGINNING_OF_TIME_STEP_PREDICTION strategy (the
  other strategies use the consistent tangent operator);
- in parallel, a non collective exception is reported on the standard
  error stream with the rank of the process, then MPI_Abort is called
  (the error stream of mfem-mgis is disabled on the other processes);
- the linear solver of the elastic operator is set up before the previous
  elastic operator is replaced, the elastic operator being computed again
  after a failure; `None` removes the linear solver of the elastic
  operator; Anderson's method is not applied for non finite coefficients;
- documentation of PredictionLinearSolver;
- FixedPointSolverTest: NewtonK0 (same iterations as Newton), predictions
  made by the linear solver given by the fixed point solver (counted by a
  linear solver of the test), refusals of the new combinations.
